{title: Three Quarter Time}
{artist: Songbook Demo}
{level: Easy}
{duration: 2.2}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 108}
{strum: waltz-3-4}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]Count the evening [C]slowly, [G]one and two and [D]three
[G]Every quiet [C]corner [G]keeps a [D]waltz for [G]me
[G]Take the hand of [C]morning, [G]turn beneath the [D]sky
[G]Leave the heavy [C]hours [G]dancing [D]by and [G]by

{comment: Chorus}
[C]Three quarter [G]time, [C]three quarter [G]time
[Em]All of the [D]world in a [C]small happy [G]rhyme
[C]Three quarter [G]time, [C]three quarter [G]time
[Em]Carry me [D]home when the [C]bells have gone [G]quiet
